<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Greatest area of a pen against a wall</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(cx=0)"]]Wambui has \({@L0@}\) m of wire fencing to make a rectangular chicken run against the wall of her house in Nyeri.[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]Moraa has \({@L0@}\) m of wire fencing to make a rectangular kitchen garden against a stone wall in Kisii.[[elif test="is(cx=2)"]]Sankale has \({@L0@}\) m of wire fencing to make a rectangular calf pen against the wall of a store in Narok.[[else]]Kariuki has \({@L0@}\) m of wire fencing to make a rectangular drying area for coffee beans against the wall of a store in Murang'a.[[/if]] The wall forms one side, so the fence makes the other three. Let \(x\) m be the length of each side that meets the wall.</p><p>(a) Write the area \(A\) \(\text{m}^2\) in terms of \(x\).</p><div>\(A =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the value of \(x\) that gives the greatest area.</p><div>\(x =\) [[input:ans2]] m [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the greatest area.</p><div>[[input:ans3]] \(\text{m}^2\) [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The best value of a quantity is at a stationary point or at an end of its domain.</p><p>(a) Two sides of \(x\) m use \(2x\) m of fence, so the side along the wall is \({@L0-2*x@}\) m and \(A = {@Am@} = {@expand(Am)@}\), with \(0 \lt x \lt {@L0/2@}\).</p><p>(b) \(\dfrac{dA}{dx} = {@diff(expand(Am),x)@} = 0\) when \(x = {@xb@}\). \(\dfrac{d^2A}{dx^2} = -4 \lt 0\), so this gives the greatest area.</p><p>(c) The pen is \({@xb@}\) m by \({@yb@}\) m, and \(A = {@xb@} \times {@yb@} = {@Ab@}\) \(\text{m}^2\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_x(ex) := if every(lambda([v], member(v, [x])), listofvars(ex)) then "" else "Use x as the only letter in your answer.";
/* Design: fencing three sides against a wall, with a randomised length. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 1, chapter 9, Exercise D question 3. */
ix: 1+rand(10);
L0: [24,28,32,36,40,44,48,52,56,64][ix];
cx: rand(4);
Am: x*(L0-2*x);
xb: L0/4; Ab: L0^2/8; yb: L0/2;
Aone: x*(L0-x); Afour: x*(L0/2-x);
x2: L0/2; Asq: L0^2/16; Aone2: L0^2/4;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
