  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Differentiation II: greatest area of a pen against a wall</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 4.1: Model the area of a rectangle fenced on three sides against a wall, and find the dimensions and the greatest area.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 3 in Exercise D of Chapter 9 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: a wall instead of a hedge, Kenyan contexts and a randomised length of fencing, with diagnostic feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
